{
 "id": "2026-10-14-simon-turns-mazatlan",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A hurricane that stalled for days is turning toward a resort city. Is Mazatlán next?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Simon is strengthening again, nearly a major hurricane, the U.S. hurricane center said. On Tuesday morning it was about two hundred ten miles south-southwest of Mazatlán, and should approach Mexico's west-central coast Wednesday into Thursday."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Mexico's weather service issued a hurricane warning from Jalisco to Nayarit, including the Islas Marías. A hurricane watch covers the coast up to Sinaloa, which includes Mazatlán. Waves of up to five meters have damaged its seafront, local media report."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "The Associated Press says the death toll from Simon and the remnants of storm Rachel has risen to six. A Mexican civil protection official said Simon could hit Mazatlán as a category one hurricane. Earlier forecasts have shifted."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Simon make landfall in Sinaloa? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
